{"id": "EUVD-2026-107420", "enisaUuid": "97068c8a-0fe9-39ed-be49-ac2654f753a4", "description": "gin-vue-admin through 2.9.2 contains a path traversal vulnerability that allows authenticated administrators to recursively delete arbitrary directories by supplying traversal sequences in the pluginName parameter. Attackers can send a crafted POST request to /autoCode/removePlugin with '../' sequences, causing os.RemoveAll to delete any directory writable by the server process.", "datePublished": "2026-10-21T17:54:16", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T17:54:16", "baseScore": 7.0, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:H/UI:N/VC:N/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/flipped-aurora/gin-vue-admin/security/advisories/GHSA-mqv7-9mvf-h9fh", "https://github.com/flipped-aurora/gin-vue-admin/blob/v2.9.2-stable/server/service/system/auto_code_plugin.go#L371-L390", "https://github.com/flipped-aurora/gin-vue-admin/blob/v2.9.2-stable/server/api/v1/system/auto_code_plugin.go#L209-L219", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/gin-vue-admin-through-2.9.2-path-traversal-via-removeplugin-endpoint"], "aliases": ["GHSA-qgwp-mwx4-c64g", "CVE-2026-114492"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.42, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "d9be8d1a-2d10-381a-8cca-5794ba681917", "product": {"name": "gin-vue-admin", "vendor": {"name": "flipped-aurora"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22642.9.2"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "32258085-c67f-3f90-ab10-1f828a6ac716", "vendor": {"name": "flipped-aurora"}}], "isExploited": false}